type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381618} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97bc66f3-590f-5bd4-83b8-ff95c3d4d3a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≡" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381622} {:answer/id #uuid "1cee7a75-74b5-56c0-ba00-d1f44e16aef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≢" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cee7a75-74b5-56c0-ba00-d1f44e16aef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≢" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381623} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9983ec7-ca56-595b-9e12-4b8bda085077" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2ddf2c6-0317-53dd-890e-de5a25799da4" :question/math-academy-id "q-182488" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-3}} | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n¬(P∨Q){{field-4}}¬P∨Q\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∨Q) & ≡¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬P∨Q & ≡¬\\text{T}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(P∨Q) & ≡¬(\\text{F}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬(P∨Q)\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $¬(P∨Q)$ is logically equivalent to $¬P∨Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are *different* (one is $\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{T}$, while the other is $\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T}$). Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬(P∨Q)\\text{⧸}≢¬P∨Q.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186376279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a6a36e8-e14e-5051-acae-48de63ff3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Statements Using Partially Completed Truth Tables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da3e1819-be60-5a6f-af97-3cfbf3ede66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376281} {:answer/id #uuid "b7fcaf27-646e-5d5b-8436-df7bd028b411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7fcaf27-646e-5d5b-8436-df7bd028b411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376282} :answer-field/id #uuid "d886e475-422e-56ab-8b7f-3d60083870f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376280} {:answ