n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $¬(A∧¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $¬A∨B,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n¬(A∧¬B)≡¬A∨B.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a6a36e8-e14e-5051-acae-48de63ff3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Statements Using Partially Completed Truth Tables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1843c7c7-429a-52e4-a053-a385556510ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570925} {:answer/id #uuid "38ed73c4-7b08-5bb6-86a4-3da74948ecb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38ed73c4-7b08-5bb6-86a4-3da74948ecb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570979} :answer-field/id #uuid "1562b94f-b92a-51be-82d8-44a0fe8a5bf7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c4207c3-5d89-5e1b-a6de-81a689a34ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571038} {:answer/id #uuid "c35e7574-b8be-58ca-bde9-d14d5025bb20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c35e7574-b8be-58ca-bde9-d14d5025b