 #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8916118b-53b3-5d09-94d6-cc82ce4ab29d" :question/math-academy-id "q-182516" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q){{field-4}}Q\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P\\text{ }∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{T}∨\\text{T})∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{T}$ and $Q≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{T}∨\\text{F})∧¬(\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $P≡\\text{F}$ and $Q≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q) & ≡(\\text{F}∨\\text{T})∧¬(\\text{F}∧¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)$ is logically equivalent to $Q,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{T},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(P∨Q)∧¬(P∧¬Q)≡Q.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411115 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a6a36e8-e14e-5051-acae-48de63ff3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Statements Using Partially Completed Truth Tables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "052a7912-8d7b-5fff-90e2-505d9e98c792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411068} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa51d9-b623-50fa-a3e4-46b5949bdc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "052a7912-8d7b-5fff-90e2-505d9e98c792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411068} :answer-field/id #uuid "35f1d21e-f525-5bb3-81dc-dc1d4446e2c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411103} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982e3f94-5d77-5176-9dd4-506289458c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411088} {:answer/id #uuid "db755250-bc21-584c-bdb8-21fc812b84ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "982e3f94-5d77-5176-9dd4-506289458c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411088} :answer-field/id #uuid "46669123-e51d-59ed-bd9d-af7b5c1b87de" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d8ab9c9-3b6e-506c-b947-40d6834bbb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≡" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411089} {:answer/id #uuid "e635ecab-3c5c-52ff-926d-41857ac215dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≢" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e635ecab-3c5c-52ff-926d-41857ac215dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "≢" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411099} :answer-field/id #uuid "581c9f72-306d-54b6-94af-e6d8a7a94201" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "370f4c3f-99c1-5afb-8d47-cb9a74d1c85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411072} {:answer/id #uuid "791854e7-a7e6-524b-b5e9-1dc27fcbd843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "370f4c3f-99c1-5afb-8d47-cb9a74d1c85e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{F}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411072} :answer-field/id #uuid "d440bf3f-9095-5263-9a45-107c23d37fbf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ca1a18-e271-54de-8d6a-f0aa14857b82" :question/math-academy-id "q-182517" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B){{field-4}}A\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{F}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $A,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nWe see that the columns for $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ and $A$ are different. They differ in the second and third rows. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)≢A.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a6a36e8-e14e-5051-acae-48de63ff3eff" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equivalent Statements Using Partially Completed Truth Tables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b790e6-bfc7-5680-adfc-00f8a8ce7b5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.