\  & ≡\\text{T}∧(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧B & ≡\\text{T}∧\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A∧(B∨¬A) & ≡\\text{F}∧(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧(B∨¬A)\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $A∧(B∨¬A)$ is logically equivalent to $A∧B,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.  \n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\text{T},\\text{F},\\text{F},\\text{F}).$ Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\nA∧(B∨¬A)≡A∧B.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d9123f6-1ac3-577d-8448-fa5f35090fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477461} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5ec496-8711-51ea-967c-940ed57f12cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f5ec496-8711-51ea-967c-940ed57f12cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477462} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41e8230-3016-56f5-9ecd-0c0ca53982c9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9f76af-3775-5573-8674-5ed519df7677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477463} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b32afa-ec9b-50ed-9315-54748539b4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3b32afa-ec9b-50ed-9315-54748539b4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9bb9216-5611-5306-b6e2-7e2dbeb9f076" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2422dd1-c3e9-5d60-8594-d85ecf4d1266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477465} {:answer/id #uuid "2d788219-eebe-5d12-9e1f-57b8008ed228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2422dd1-c3e9-5d60-8594-d85ecf4d1266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477465} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb1ad31-5edb-5c7d-ae51-d6dab75641d2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7074b983-3ace-5190-bf87-4742f8c8239b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81053" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n- **I.** $¬A∧B$\n- **II.** $¬(A∨¬B)$\n- **III.** $A∨¬B$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬A∧B$ and $¬(A∨¬B)$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d48f791-cfb2-5905-8a08-ac3a02cb98d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471651} {:answer/id #uuid "42a831ec-5eee-5950-80a9-6df9cae47ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42a831ec-5eee-5950-80a9-6df9cae47ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471652} :answer-field/id #uuid "895886fe-f51a-5925-af30-4f44e0e9cea8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472331}