cked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∧¬B)\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∨B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬(A∧¬B)$ and $¬A∨B$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cadf2b3a-2887-51a1-ac9a-6a100a720148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471777} {:answer/id #uuid "13acb438-be49-5b43-9f6b-58f9715282b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13acb438-be49-5b43-9f6b-58f9715282b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471778} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5593c75-ada1-59d7-8a43-cb5af290a565" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d234654d-a06c-5b98-870a-02f1f2e9cf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471779} {:answer/id #uuid "f29aac37-329c-5783-b10b-4b6a4d478e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d234654d-a06c-5b98-870a-02f1f2e9cf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471779} :answer-field/id #uuid "13849d25-31be-5849-8b24-d650f4eb32c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "263de33c-6795-58ce-85ae-92a97254075c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471781} {:answer/id #uuid "47908abc-c854-5546-bdc1-39309bb92cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47908abc-c854-5546-bdc1-39309bb92cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471782} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca92a53d-50d7-5e4b-8ec5-4c9924570bd9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17f91135-f9d8-56cf-88b5-eaf7c61a4e5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86690" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n- **I.** $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$\n- **II.** $¬X∨(X∧¬Y)$\n- **III.** $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬X∧(X∨¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬X∨(X∧¬Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬X∧(X∨¬Y)$ and $¬(X∨(¬X∧Y))$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
